Based on OpenSign
-----------------

DocuStamp began as a fork of OpenSign (https://github.com/OpenSignLabs/OpenSign),
copyright its authors (OpenSign Labs and the OpenSign contributors), licensed
under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3.
The fork point is OpenSign version 2.37.0 (upstream commit a5456dadc, August 2026).
LICENSE holds the unmodified text of the GNU AGPL, version 3. OpenSign's copy of
that file opened with the following statement, reproduced here unchanged:

    * All content that resides under the "apps/OpenSignServer/cloud/customRoute" directory of this repository, if that directory exists, is licensed under the license defined in "apps/OpenSignServer/cloud/customRoute".
    * All third party components incorporated into the OpenSign Software are licensed under the original license provided by the owner of the applicable component.
    * Content outside of the above mentioned directories or restrictions above is available under the "GNU AFFERO GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE" as defined below -

The directory it refers to does not exist in DocuStamp; that code now lives in
apps/server/cloud/routes.

Since then the code has been modified substantially, including:

  - a new web app (apps/web) replacing the original frontend;
  - a REST API (/api/v1), personal API tokens, webhooks and an MCP server;
  - optional AI document preparation;
  - security hardening across the server, and a self-signed signing
    certificate created on first boot when none is configured;
  - the server moved from apps/OpenSignServer to apps/server, and the product
    renamed to DocuStamp.

The full history of changes since the fork point is in this repository's git log.


